Size the web canvas from devicePixelContentBoxSize only where it agrees with devicePixelRatio.

What:
- gpui_web's canvas sizing trusts `devicePixelContentBoxSize` only where it agrees with the CSS box times
  `devicePixelRatio`: scale emulation (DevTools' device mode, CDP `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`,
  Playwright's `deviceScaleFactor`, in Chromium and Firefox) scales the ratio but not that box, so GPUI drew at the
  square of the scale and holes landed 1.25x off at 1.25.

Tests: scripts/web-checks.mjs's `native-view` suite at scale 1.25 (CDP `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`), which
checks the hole lands on the view (docs/native-view-web.md). Independent of patch 0054: applies before or after it.

Why: under scale emulation GPUI sized its canvas for scale 1 and drew at the square of the scale; the sizing is
private to gpui_web's window (no extension point).

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

